{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey security deposit cap","requirement":"A landlord may not hold a security deposit (including any pet deposit) above one and one-half times one month's rent, may not raise it more than 10% a year, and may take at most two and one-half times monthly rent including first month's rent.","key_value":"1.5 times one month's rent; yearly increase max 10%; 2.5 times monthly rent at inception","coverage_conditions":"All residential rental units in New Jersey; collecting a security deposit is optional but capped when collected.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit trust account, interest and account notice","requirement":"A landlord must hold deposit money in trust in an insured New Jersey interest-bearing account (ten or more units may use an insured money market fund), pay the interest to the tenant annually, and give the tenant the account details within 30 days.","key_value":"10 units; interest paid annually","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey where a landlord receives security deposit money.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Account rules differ for landlords receiving deposits for 10 or more units"},"exemptions":"Security deposits for seasonal use or rental of not more than 125 consecutive days; farm-worker housing is not seasonal use.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19","quoted_span":"A landlord or designee who receives security deposit money for ten or less units must deposit that money in an insured bank or savings and loan association located in New Jersey in an interest-bearing account at the current interest rate at the time of deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant remedy for unpaid deposit interest or missing notice","requirement":"If the landlord fails to give the required deposit notice or pay interest, the tenant may by written notice apply the deposit plus 7% annual interest to rent; for a missed annual notice or interest payment the landlord has 30 days to comply first.","key_value":"7% per annum","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey where a security deposit was collected.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Once the deposit is applied to rent, the landlord may not demand an additional security deposit.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19.1","quoted_span":"If a tenant does not receive proper notice or is not paid interest as required, the tenant may use the security deposit for payment of rent by giving the landlord written notice that the security money plus interest at the rate of 7% per annum be applied to rent payments or payments due or to become due from the tenant.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return deadline and double-damages remedy","requirement":"Within 30 days after a tenancy ends, a landlord must return the deposit plus interest less itemized deductions; if the tenant is displaced by fire, flood, condemnation or evacuation, the deposit must be returned within five business days.","key_value":"30 days; 5 business days after displacement","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey; itemized deductions must be sent by registered or certified mail.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Tenant may sue for double the amount wrongfully withheld, plus court costs and reasonable attorney’s fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Within 30 days after the termination of a tenancy, a landlord must return the security deposit, plus interest earned less deductions, to the tenant ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Safe Housing Act deposit return after domestic violence termination","requirement":"When a tenant ends a lease under the Safe Housing Act because of domestic violence, the landlord must make the deposit plus interest available within 15 business days and notify the tenant within three business days of when and where to collect it.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Leases terminated by a domestic violence victim under the Safe Housing Act (N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.4 et seq.).","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"If a tenant terminates the lease agreement prior to the expiration of the lease pursuant to the Safe Housing Act , (N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6), the tenant is entitled to the return of their security deposit. Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
